doc_version()` (already used at test_wiki_render_hardening.py:479) as the intended mechanism.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.834,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'the comment naming a specific version string and the method used to extract it'","Repo already uses `pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()` at test_wiki_render_hardening.py:479 and scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py:494,544","Plan Approach says only 'The pinned wheel's bundled pandoc version must be determined' without naming a method"],"finding":"AC1 requires identifying the pandoc version bundled in pypandoc-binary==1.17 and recording 'the method used to extract it', but the plan proposes no method and does not cite the directly applicable API the repo already uses. `pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()` is invoked at test_wiki_render_hardening.py:479 and scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py — a one-line, already-vetted way to extract the bundled version. Leaving the extraction method fully open is a small feasibility gap given a known-good method exists in-tree.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4195a8728a132652","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — AC1 ('pandoc version bundled in pypandoc-binary==1.17 is identified')","norm_id":"n2327d09616a0b7e3","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor invents an ad-hoc extraction (unzipping the wheel and running the binary, which cannot run on arm64) instead of the trivial in-env `pypandoc.get_pandoc_version()`."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Strengthen AC2's proving command to anchor on the specific added section (e.g. grep for a distinctive heading or the phrase 'arm64 macOS hosts require a system pandoc') rather than two independent substring greps.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.73,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["AC2: \"grep -qi 'arm64' docs/local-dev-env.md && grep -qi 'pandoc' docs/local-dev-env.md\"","Verify-command taxonomy item (4) fixture invalidity / (1) substring false-positive"],"finding":"AC2's verification uses two independent case-insensitive greps (`grep -qi 'arm64'` and `grep -qi 'pandoc'`) that can match unrelated occurrences anywhere in the file rather than confirming a coherent section documenting the arm64 pandoc requirement.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f91313ae3219bdc10","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC2)","norm_id":"n21157cae0004edd0","priority":0.22,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["docs already mention arm64 and pandoc separately in unrelated contexts, passing grep without the required section existing"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Replace with a single anchored check, e.g. `grep -qiE 'arm64[^\\n]*pandoc|pandoc[^\\n]*arm64' docs/local-dev-env.md` or grep for the exact heading text you add.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm and record pypandoc==1.17's actual get_pandoc_path resolution semantics — that a PATH pandoc is preferred over the bundled binary AND accepted only if executable — rather than relying on the quoted search_paths line alone.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4284,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan quotes: search_paths = [\"pandoc\", included_pandoc] and asserts 'the resolver accepts only a candidate it can actually invoke'","wiki_render._pandoc_path() at src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira_family/wiki_render.py:144-145 simply returns str(pypandoc.get_pandoc_path()) — the entire remedy depends on pypandoc's internal resolution","AC #3 verifies the OUTCOME (get_pandoc_path prints an arm64 path) but the plan does not confirm the MECHANISM claim about executability-verification vs. existence-only resolution"],"finding":"The approach's correctness hinges entirely on the unstated-but-quoted claim that pypandoc's resolver consults PATH before the bundled binary AND 'accepts only a candidate it can actually invoke' (executability check, not mere existence). If pypandoc instead resolves by existence, or tries the bundled path first in any code path, or caches a stale path, a system arm64 pandoc would NOT win and the no-product-code remedy fails silently. The plan should verify this specific pypandoc behavior for the pinned pypandoc-binary==1.17 and record the exact resolution semantics, not just quote the search_paths list.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa166339bb56b1a22","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section","norm_id":"n3fcb839565eda164","priority":0.1716,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A developer has a broken/non-executable pandoc on PATH; if pypandoc resolves by existence it returns that path and tests fail differently","pypandoc caches the bundled path from an earlier import in the same process before PATH pandoc is installed"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.65,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the exact `pypandoc` version whose `_ensure_pandoc_path()` source was read for the quoted `search_paths = [\"pandoc\", included_pandoc]` order, and confirm it is the version the `wiki` extra/lock installs, so the PATH-first resolution the remedy depends on is verified against a stated surface.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.7284,"drop_reason":"novelty","evidence":["Plan quotes `search_paths = [\"pandoc\", included_pandoc]` and asserts 'A pandoc on PATH is consulted before the bundled binary'","`pypandoc` is UNRESOLVED in the review probe env; the plan names no pypandoc version for the quoted internal","`_ensure_pandoc_path` is a private pypandoc internal not searchable in this repo (search returned no matches), so the quote is unverified against a stated version","pypandoc IS confirmed a real, already-used integration: `pypandoc.get_pandoc_path()`/`get_pandoc_version()` at test_wiki_render_hardening.py:479 and scripts/generate_dc_wiki_legacy_outputs.py"],"finding":"The remedy's load-bearing claim — that pypandoc consults a PATH `pandoc` before the bundled binary via `_ensure_pandoc_path()` with `search_paths = [\"pandoc\", included_pandoc]` — is presented as observed source but is not attributed to a specific pypandoc version. pypandoc's resolver internals (a private function and its search-order structure) can change across releases; the entire 'fixable without changing any product code' approach depends on this exact behavior holding for the pypandoc version resolved by the wiki extra. Ground the claim by naming the pypandoc version whose source was read (and confirming it matches the version the lock/extra actually installs), so the mechanism is Verified against a stated surface rather than recalled.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5b314a837c47f5b5","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach section — quoted `search_paths = [\"pandoc\", included_pandoc]`","norm_id":"ncb6f7379dac1578a","priority":0.1716,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The pypandoc version installed by the wiki extra resolves the executable differently (e.g. bundled-first, or no PATH consultation), so a system arm64 pandoc never wins and the 17 tests still fail after all the doc work is shipped."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.65,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"69a5ebc25a9eafd9","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["cd140c13c02e0250",5495],"description_boxes":["8b6fa01313ce51af",0],"file_impact":["fd9c7408579ce566",1],"ticket_id":["bf22240c6fe1d543",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":229744,"cache_write_tokens":76801,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":3721.1,"input_tokens":327087,"llm_calls":27,"llm_ms":182233.2,"output_tokens":22145,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":193300.4,"verify_requests":14},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.clau